 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 667117,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following results in a 2 by 3 <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ndarray</code>?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1330312,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">import numpy as np\narr = np.array(2, 3)\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "When creating an <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ndarray</code> object, dimensions are passed as a tuple."
    },
    {
     "id": 1330313,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">import numpy as np\narr = np.array([[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]])\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">np.array([[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]])</code> creates an <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ndarray</code> of 3 by 2. How to convert a 3 by 2 <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ndarray</code> to a 2 by 3?"
    },
    {
     "id": 1330314,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">import numpy as np\narr = np.array([[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]]).T\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">np.array([[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]])</code> creates an <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ndarray</code> of 3 by 2. The <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">T</code> operator transposes the array. The transpose operator takes an array of <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">m</code> by <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">n</code> and converts the array to an <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">n</code> by <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">m</code> array. The result of applying the transpose operator on the given array is a 2 by 3 array."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
